+/* mGBA Dual: two GBA instances of the same ROM in ONE libretro core,
+ * connected by mGBA's lockstep SIO driver (link cable).
+ *
+ * - mgba_dual_link is read only at content load (on by default). Off creates
+ *   only player 1, without a link driver, and keeps the normal .srm interface.
+ * - Both cores are stepped cooperatively on one thread: the lockstep user's
+ *   sleep/wake only flip a flag, and retro_run interleaves run-loop slices of
+ *   whichever core is awake until core 0 finishes one video frame (the same
+ *   scheme as tangobattle/mgba-rollback). The whole link is therefore a
+ *   deterministic function of the two joypads, which is exactly what plain
+ *   RetroArch netplay (input sync + rollback) needs.
+ * - Port 0 drives core 0 (player 1 / host), port 1 drives core 1 (player 2 /
+ *   guest). The "mgba_dual_screen" option only picks whose picture and sound
+ *   are output; it never touches emulation state.
+ * - Player 1's save is RETRO_MEMORY_SAVE_RAM (the normal .srm). Player 2's
+ *   save lives in <save dir>/<rom>.p2.srm, written by this core (never in 2P
+ *   mode, where the save belongs to the host).
+ * - retro_serialize stores both cores, both lockstep driver blobs (player 0's
+ *   blob carries the coordinator), both save buffers, and the few pieces of
+ *   state that mGBA's savestate encodes lossily (audio FIFO countdown, DMA
+ *   control), in a fixed-size, zero-filled layout. */
